abstract: >-
  Batch renaming of scientific paper PDFs from their own bibliographic
  metadata: a graphical tool that identifies each file via the Crossref
  API, then renames it according to a customisable pattern built from
  year, first author, title, journal and user-defined tags — with a
  built-in database of about 30,000 journal abbreviations, a live
  preview before anything is changed, and a manual fallback when the
  lookup fails. Turns an ad-hoc pile of downloads into a consistently
  named, searchable local literature collection.
  Funded by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG, German Research
  Foundation) under the National Research Data Infrastructure –
  NFDI 38/1 – project number 460247524 (NFDI-MatWerk consortium).
